**Current Requirements:**
```
SYSTEM OVERVIEW
===============
The system is a Role-based Access Control (RBAC) environment supporting multiple users, role hierarchies, temporary role delegation, revocation, and concurrent request processing. The system enforces authorization correctness, maintains delegation and permission consistency, and ensures safety and liveness under concurrency. Users have clearance levels (High, Medium, Low), and objects have classification levels (High, Medium, Low). Requests are classified by the highest classification level of affected objects and must comply with user clearance. Higher-clearance users can approve or reject lower-clearance user requests. Delegation and revocation of roles are governed by clearance and administrative rules. The system includes an Emergency Module to manage exceptional scenarios, which alters standard behaviors under specific triggers and constraints. Emergency mode is modeled as a fixed duration but may terminate early if both administrators who activated it jointly deactivate it. The system guarantees that Emergency mode always eventually ends and the system returns to Normal mode.

EXISTING-SYSTEM ASSUMPTIONS AND CONSTRAINTS
============================================
- Administrator membership is fixed; a user is an administrator if and only if they are in the Administrator set. isAdmin = True if and only if the user is an Administrator. Administrator status must be explicitly represented in the model.
- Emergency mode can only be triggered from Normal mode and requires exactly two distinct administrators (emAdmins), both present in Administrator, acting concurrently to trigger entry. There is no requirement that two administrators must always exist in every session. The absence of sufficient administrators in a session must prevent Emergency mode entry, but does not violate any system invariant.
- Emergency mode is time-bounded (abstracted as a fixed duration), but may terminate early if both participating administrators jointly deactivate it; the system must always eventually return to Normal mode (liveness).
- FIFO ordering for request processing can be bypassed only during Emergency mode, and only for high-classification requests.
- Mutual exclusivity of roles is suspended only during Emergency mode, and only if two distinct emAdmins are present; this suspension must be tested as a specific scenario.
- Emergency privileges are granted only to the two distinct administrators who jointly triggered Emergency mode, only during Emergency mode, and must be revoked immediately at the transition to Normal mode for both administrators and in all subsequent Normal states.
- Roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked immediately at the Emergency-to-Normal transition. Roles delegated prior to Emergency mode are not automatically revoked, but may still expire or be revoked by an administrator during Emergency mode.
- Only the two administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger are required to update their credentials after Emergency mode ends; needsCredentialUpdate is set for them only in the first Normal state after Emergency mode ends, and must be unset (empty) in all other states.
- There is no constraint on the total number of administrators present in any session; the requirement for two emAdmins applies only to Emergency mode entry.

PROSPECTIVE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
====================================
R1: Emergency Trigger  
Exactly two distinct administrators, both present in the Administrator set and acting concurrently while the system is in Normal mode, are required to jointly trigger entry into Emergency mode. "Exactly two distinct" means the set of emAdmins must have cardinality two, both must be members of Administrator, and both must be distinct (no duplicates by signature). Emergency mode entry must be impossible in all other administrator configurations: with fewer than two administrators, with more than two administrators, with duplicate (identical) administrators, or with any non-administrator. All such cases—including attempted entry by only one administrator, by the same administrator counted twice, by more than two administrators, or by any non-admin—must be encoded and verified as explicit negative test scenarios using scenario predicates with `expect 0`, and shown to be disallowed by the model. The system must demonstrate that Emergency mode is possible only when exactly two distinct emAdmins act concurrently.

R2: Emergency Mode Duration  
Emergency mode is active only for a limited (bounded) time, abstracted as a fixed duration, but may terminate early if both participating emAdmins jointly deactivate Emergency. The system must always eventually terminate Emergency mode and return to Normal mode (liveness guarantee).

R3: Emergency Mode Behavior  
R3.1. During Emergency mode, request processing may bypass FIFO order to prioritize and process multiple high-classification requests simultaneously.  
R3.2. During Emergency mode, users may temporarily hold roles that are normally mutually exclusive, but only when two distinct emAdmins are present. This scenario must be specifically tested.  
R3.3. During Emergency mode, only the two distinct administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger temporarily hold emergency privileges, and only during Emergency mode.

R4: Post-Emergency Restoration  
R4.1. After Emergency mode ends, emergency privileges must be revoked immediately for both administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger, starting from the first Normal state and in all subsequent Normal states. EmergencyPrivilege for both emAdmins must not be present in any Normal state after Emergency mode ends.
R4.2. After Emergency mode ends, any roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked immediately. Delegated roles from before Emergency mode remain subject to normal expiration or administrator revocation, including during Emergency mode.  
R4.3. After Emergency mode ends, needsCredentialUpdate must be set to true for only the two administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger, and only in the first Normal state after Emergency mode ends. needsCredentialUpdate must be empty (false for all users) in all other states, including during Emergency mode and all other Normal states.

NEWLY DISCOVERED REQUIREMENT GAPS
==================================
- All negative test scenarios for Emergency mode entry (fewer than two administrators, more than two administrators, duplicates, non-admins, or lack of concurrency) must be defined as explicit scenario predicates, each with `expect 0` to ensure no instance is possible. These must be run and verified in the model.
- The system must avoid vacuity in test scenarios: negative scenarios must be encoded as explicit scenario predicates with `expect 0`, and the positive scenario (exactly two distinct emAdmins) as an assertion or predicate with `expect 1`, to demonstrate model rejection or acceptance as required.
- Emergency mode entry and all related behaviors and suspensions (such as mutual exclusivity) are predicated on the presence of exactly two distinct emAdmins; these preconditions must be enforced and explicitly tested.

PROVISIONAL ASSUMPTIONS FOR VERIFICATION
========================================
- For purposes of verification, scenarios with fewer than two, exactly two, more than two, duplicate, and non-admin administrators attempting to trigger Emergency mode are explicitly modeled as separate edge cases. Only the case with exactly two distinct emAdmins acting concurrently may result in Emergency mode being entered; all others must not.
- For concurrency modeling, "acting concurrently" is abstracted as a single transition step for both administrators.
- Constraints on the number and identity of administrators participating in Emergency mode entry are enforced through explicit scenario predicates and negative test cases, rather than by restricting the administrator count in command signatures. This avoids syntax errors and improves clarity.
```

**Current Alloy Model:**
```alloy
// ===== RBAC Emergency Model (Alloy 6, Abstract, Requirements-conformant, Emergency Edge Cases) =====

open util/ordering[State] as Time

// ===== ENUMS AND MODES =====

abstract sig Bool {}
one sig True, False extends Bool {}

abstract sig ClearanceLevel {}
one sig High, Medium, Low extends ClearanceLevel {}

abstract sig ClassificationLevel {}
one sig C_High, C_Medium, C_Low extends ClassificationLevel {}

abstract sig SystemMode {}
one sig Normal, Emergency extends SystemMode {}

// ===== CORE ENTITIES =====

sig User {
    clearance: one ClearanceLevel,
    isAdmin: one Bool
}

sig Administrator in User {}

sig Role {
    mutuallyExclusiveWith: set Role
}

sig Object {
    classification: one ClassificationLevel
}

sig Request {
    requestedBy: one User,
    affects: some Object,
    classification: one ClassificationLevel
}

sig Delegation {
    delegatee: one User,
    role: one Role,
    delegatedAt: one State,
    expiresAt: lone State
}

sig EmergencyPrivilege {
    admin: one Administrator,
    grantedAt: one State,
    revokedAt: lone State
}

// ===== SYSTEM STATE =====

sig State {
    mode: one SystemMode,
    emAdmins: set Administrator, // exactly 2 when entering Emergency, else empty
    requests: set Request,
    delegations: set Delegation,
    emPrivs: set EmergencyPrivilege,
    needsCredentialUpdate: set Administrator
}

// ===== SYSTEM INVARIANTS and BASELINE FACTS =====

// isAdmin iff membership in Administrator
fact R0_IsAdminIffAdministrator {
    all u: User | (u in Administrator) iff (u.isAdmin = True)
}

// All Administrators have High clearance and isAdmin True
fact R0_AdminDefinition {
    all a: Administrator | a.clearance = High and a.isAdmin = True
    all u: User - Administrator | u.isAdmin = False
}

// ===== Emergency Mode Entry: Only possible with exactly 2 distinct emAdmins in Administrator, triggered from Normal =====
fact R1_EmergencyEntry_Strict {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s]) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and s.emAdmins in Administrator)
        else
            (s.mode = Emergency) => (#Time/prev[s].emAdmins = 2 and Time/prev[s].emAdmins in Administrator)
}

// EmergencyPrivilege: only for the two emAdmins, only during Emergency; none persists in any Normal state
fact R3_3_EmergencyPrivilegeAssignment_And_Revocation {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (all ep: s.emPrivs |
                ep.admin in s.emAdmins and ep.grantedAt = s and no ep.revokedAt)
            and
            (all a: s.emAdmins | some ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin = a and ep.grantedAt = s)
        else
            no s.emPrivs
}

// needsCredentialUpdate: set to both emAdmins only in first Normal after Emergency, empty in all other states
fact R4_3_EmergencyCredentialUpdate_Strict {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            s.needsCredentialUpdate = Time/prev[s].emAdmins
        else
            no s.needsCredentialUpdate
}

// Delegation revocation: all delegations assigned during Emergency must be revoked at Emergency->Normal
fact R4_2_EmergencyDelegationRevocation {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: s.delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => d.expiresAt = s
}

// Delegations from before Emergency are not revoked automatically
fact R4_2b_DelegationsNotRevokedIfBeforeEmergency {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: s.delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) => (no d.expiresAt or d.expiresAt != s)
}

// Request classification equals highest classification of affected objects
fact F_RequestClassification {
    all req: Request |
        req.classification = highestClass[req.affects]
}

// FIFO enforced except for C_High requests during Emergency
fact F_FIFOEnforcedExceptEmergency {
    all s: State |
        s.mode = Normal => FIFOProcessing[s]
}

// Mutual exclusion enforced in Normal; suspended only in Emergency with exactly two emAdmins
fact F_MutualExclusionEnforced {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal =>
            all u: User |
                all r1, r2: Role |
                    (r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r1 != r2) =>
                        not (r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith)
        )
}

// Emergency mode must always eventually end (liveness)
fact R2_EmergencyLiveness {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) => some s2: State | gt[s2, s] and s2.mode = Normal
}

// ==== Helper functions and predicates ====

// Returns the roles held by user u at state s
fun rolesHeld[u: User, s: State]: set Role {
    { r: Role |
        some d: s.delegations |
            d.delegatee = u and
            d.role = r and
            d.delegatedAt in pastOrEqual[s] and
            (no d.expiresAt or lt[s, d.expiresAt])
    }
}

// Returns all states up to and including s
fun pastOrEqual[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | lte[s2, s] } }

// Highest classification of a set of objects
fun highestClass[os: set Object]: one ClassificationLevel {
    (some o: os | o.classification = C_High) => C_High
    else (some o: os | o.classification = C_Medium) => C_Medium
    else C_Low
}

// FIFO abstract predicate
pred FIFOProcessing[s: State] {}

// Bypass FIFO for C_High requests during Emergency
pred bypassFIFOForHighClass[s: State] {
    all r: s.requests |
        (r.classification = C_High) => canBeProcessedOutOfOrder[r, s]
}

// During Emergency, C_High requests may be processed out of order
pred canBeProcessedOutOfOrder[r: Request, s: State] {
    r in s.requests and s.mode = Emergency and r.classification = C_High
}

// Mutual exclusion not enforced during Emergency (scenario only)
pred notMutualExclusionDuringEmergency[s: State] {}

// Helper: previous mode is Normal
pred prevModeIsNormal[s: State] {
    some Time/prev[s] and Time/prev[s].mode = Normal
}

// Helper: previous mode is Emergency
pred prevModeIsEmergency[s: State] {
    some Time/prev[s] and Time/prev[s].mode = Emergency
}

// ========== REQUIREMENT PREDICATES (incremental) ==========

// R1: Emergency Trigger — only if exactly 2 distinct emAdmins, both in Administrator, from Normal
pred R1 {
    some s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s] and #s.emAdmins = 2 and
         s.emAdmins in Administrator)
    and
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s]) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and
             s.emAdmins in Administrator)
}

// R2: Emergency Mode Duration (liveness) — system always returns to Normal
pred R1R2 {
    R1 and
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) => some s2: State | gt[s2, s] and s2.mode = Normal
}

// R3: Emergency behavior (FIFO bypass, mutual exclusion suspended, em privileges granted)
pred R1R2R3 {
    R1R2 and

    // R3.1: FIFO can be bypassed for high-classification requests
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) => bypassFIFOForHighClass[s]
    and

    // R3.2: Mutual exclusion is suspended in Emergency — scenario testable via predicate
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) => notMutualExclusionDuringEmergency[s]
    and

    // R3.3: Only the two emAdmins have EmergencyPrivilege during Emergency
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (all ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin in s.emAdmins and ep.grantedAt = s and no ep.revokedAt)
            and
            (all a: s.emAdmins | some ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin = a and ep.grantedAt = s)
}

// R4: Post-Emergency Restoration (immediate revocation, credential update for emAdmins only)
pred R1R2R3R4 {
    R1R2R3 and

    // R4.1: emAdmins lose EmergencyPrivilege immediately after Emergency, in first and all subsequent Normal states
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal) =>
            no s.emPrivs

    and

    // R4.2: Only delegations assigned during Emergency are revoked when Emergency ends
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: s.delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => (d.expiresAt = s)

    and

    // R4.2b: Delegations assigned before Emergency are NOT revoked at Emergency end
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: s.delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) => (no d.expiresAt or d.expiresAt != s)

    and

    // R4.3: Only the two emAdmins must update credentials after Emergency, and only in the first Normal after Emergency. Otherwise, needsCredentialUpdate is empty.
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            s.needsCredentialUpdate = Time/prev[s].emAdmins
    and
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Emergency) or (s.mode = Normal and not prevModeIsEmergency[s])) =>
            no s.needsCredentialUpdate
}

// All requirements predicate
pred All_Requirements { R1R2R3R4 }

// ========== EDGE CASE SCENARIO PREDICATES FOR NEGATIVE/EXPLICIT TESTS ==========

// Negative: Emergency entry attempted with only one emAdmin (expect 0)
pred Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithSingleAdmin {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s] and #s.emAdmins = 1
}

// Negative: Emergency entry attempted with more than two emAdmins (expect 0)
pred Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithMoreThanTwoAdmins {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s] and #s.emAdmins > 2
}

// Negative: Emergency entry attempted with an emAdmin not in Administrator (expect 0)
pred Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithNonAdminEmAdmin {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s] and (some a: s.emAdmins | a not in Administrator)
}

// Positive: Emergency entry with exactly 2 distinct emAdmins (expect 1)
pred Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithExactlyTwoDistinctAdmins {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s] and
        #s.emAdmins = 2 and s.emAdmins in Administrator
}

// Negative: Emergency entry attempted with duplicate emAdmins (not possible in Alloy set semantics, but for traceability, check for non-distinctness)
// [EVENT]: Replaced invalid sum b: s.emAdmins | b=a with set difference and cardinality check to express duplicate detection.
pred Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithDuplicateAdmin {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s] and #s.emAdmins = 2 and
        (some a: s.emAdmins | #(s.emAdmins - a) < 1)
}

// Positive: Mutual exclusion is suspended during Emergency with exactly two distinct emAdmins present (expect 1)
pred Scenario_MutualExclusionSuspended_Positive {
    Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithExactlyTwoDistinctAdmins
    and
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and
        #s.emAdmins = 2 and
        some u: User, r1, r2: Role |
            r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
            r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s]
}

// Negative: Mutual exclusion suspended with <2 or >2 emAdmins (should be impossible, expect 0)
pred Scenario_MutualExclusionSuspended_Negative {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and
        (#s.emAdmins < 2 or #s.emAdmins > 2 or (some a: s.emAdmins | a not in Administrator)) and
        some u: User, r1, r2: Role |
            r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
            r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s]
}

// Negative: needsCredentialUpdate set outside first Normal after Emergency (expect 0)
pred Scenario_CredentialUpdateOutsidePostEmergency {
    some s: State |
        ((s.mode = Emergency) or (s.mode = Normal and not prevModeIsEmergency[s])) and
        some (s.needsCredentialUpdate)
}

// Negative: EmergencyPrivilege present in any Normal state (expect 0)
pred Scenario_EmergencyPrivilegeInNormal {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Normal and some s.emPrivs
}

// ========== ASSERTIONS FOR VERIFICATION ==========

assert assertR1 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency and prevModeIsNormal[s]) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and
             s.emAdmins in Administrator)
}

assert assertR2 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) => (some s2: State | gt[s2, s] and s2.mode = Normal)
}

assert assertR3_MutExScenario_Positive {
    Scenario_MutualExclusionSuspended_Positive
}

assert assertR4_1 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal) =>
            no s.emPrivs
}

assert assertR4_2 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: s.delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => d.expiresAt = s
}

assert assertR4_2b {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: s.delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) => (no d.expiresAt or d.expiresAt != s)
}

assert assertR4_3 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            s.needsCredentialUpdate = Time/prev[s].emAdmins
    and
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Emergency) or (s.mode = Normal and not prevModeIsEmergency[s])) =>
            no s.needsCredentialUpdate
}

assert assertIsAdminIffAdministrator {
    all u: User | (u in Administrator) iff (u.isAdmin = True)
}

// ========== RUN/CHECK/EXPECT COMMANDS ==========

run Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithExactlyTwoDistinctAdmins for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 1
run Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithSingleAdmin for 5 but 3 State, 3 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0
run Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithDuplicateAdmin for 5 but 3 State, 3 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0
run Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithNonAdminEmAdmin for 5 but 3 State, 3 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0
run Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithMoreThanTwoAdmins for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0
run Scenario_MutualExclusionSuspended_Positive for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 1
run Scenario_MutualExclusionSuspended_Negative for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0
run Scenario_CredentialUpdateOutsidePostEmergency for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0
run Scenario_EmergencyPrivilegeInNormal for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request expect 0

run R1 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
run R1R2 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
run R1R2R3 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
run R1R2R3R4 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
run All_Requirements for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request

check assertR1 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertR2 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertR3_MutExScenario_Positive for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertR4_1 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertR4_2 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertR4_2b for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertR4_3 for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request
check assertIsAdminIffAdministrator for 5 but 3 State, 4 User, 3 Role, 5 Object, 5 Request

// -- END OF MODEL --

// [EVENT]: Fixed syntax error in Scenario_EmergencyEntryWithDuplicateAdmin: replaced invalid 'sum b: s.emAdmins | b=a' with a set-based expression '(some a: s.emAdmins | #(s.emAdmins - a) < 1)' to model duplicate detection in sets.
// [EVENT]: Checked all other uses of 'sum' and found none; all quantifiers now use valid set-based or integer expressions.
// [LESSON]: Can't use 'sum b: S | b=a' to count occurrences as Alloy doesn't treat boolean as integer; must use set cardinality comparisons or conditional sum with explicit integer results.
// [EVENT]: Confirmed all scenario predicates use set semantics for quantifiers (some, all, no), not relation applications.
// [EVENT]: No further type errors or syntax issues remain after this fix.
