// -- END OF MODEL --

// [EVENT]: Added fact F_NoRoleSelfExclusion to ensure no role is mutually exclusive with itself (requirement: no self-exclusion).
// [EVENT]: Strengthened Scenario_MutualExclusionSuspended_Positive to require explicit delegation of both mutually exclusive roles to one user during Emergency with two emAdmins, ensuring non-vacuity and model realizability.
// [EVENT]: Added negative scenario predicates for mutual exclusion suspension with <2, >2, or non-admin emAdmins, and in Normal mode.
// [EVENT]: Increased scope for State, User, and Role in run/check commands to ensure enough atoms for edge case realization.
// [EVENT]: Updated R3.2 in requirements and model to demand explicit, non-vacuous demonstration that mutual exclusion suspension is exercised in Emergency with two emAdmins.
// [EVENT]: Confirmed that all mutualExclusion edge cases are encoded and checked with expect 0/1 as required.
// [LESSON]: Alloy sets are inherently duplicate-free; to express "duplicate" scenarios, must use explicit set cardinality checks or model as vacuously impossible (for traceability).
// [LESSON]: Must use set cardinality and explicit existential quantification to ensure at least one user holds two mutually exclusive roles in positive scenario; cannot rely on vacuous model structure.
// [LESSON]: In Alloy, self-exclusion in a relation must be explicitly excluded by a fact; otherwise, it is allowed by default.
